")\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Competition dates"] "\n" [:td {} "\n—\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "OCOG"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/organizations/352"} "Organizing Committee of the XIIth Olympiad Tokyo 1940"] ", " [:a {:href "/organizations/353"} "Helsinki Olympic Organizing Committee"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "\nOverview\n\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "The Games of the XIIth Olympiad were to have been held from 22 September to 6 October 1940, in Tokyo, Japan. At the 36th IOC Session in Berlin, on 31 July 1936, the Games were awarded to Tokyo, Japan, by a vote of 36-27 over Helsinki, Finland. Other cities that had expressed interest in hosting the 1940 Olympics were Alexandria, Egypt; Buenos Aires, Argentina; Dublin, Ireland; Athina, Greece; Rio de Janeiro, Brazil; Barcelona, Spain; Budapest, Hungary; and either Toronto, Ontario, or Montréal, Québec, both in Canada. The choice of Tokyo was highly controversial as it was currently occupying Manchuria in Northern China, and would shortly be involved in the Sino-Japanese war over this occupation."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the midst of the world-wide depression, Japan offered huge financial guarantees, offering to pay subsidies for each foreign team that competed. Full-scale war between Japan and China began in July 1937 and, in mid-1938, the Japanese government informed the Organizing Committees for Tokyo and Sapporo that they were withdrawing all financial support for the Olympic Games. On 16 July 1938, Tokyo withdrew as host. In the last issue of the " [:em {} "Olympic News"] ", published by the Japanese Organizing Committee, they mentioned “the trouble with China”, as the reason for their withdrawal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Helsinki had already declared it was willing to step in should Tokyo fail to organize the Games, and they informally confirmed their willingness to take over only three days after Tokyo withdrew. On 3 September 1938, at the IOC Executive Board meeting in Bruxelles, the Games were officially awarded to Helsinki. The Games were scheduled for 20 July to 4 August 1940, and all stadia were ready by late 1939, except for the swimming arena."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Olympic Programme underwent some changes, partially because of the short preparation period. Hockey, handball, and basketball were all dropped, but hang gliding, which was approved by the " [:a {:href "/organizations/1"} "IOC"] " in 1938, was a new sport. Although a (non-competitive) demonstration had been held at the " [:a {:href "/results/900065"} "1936 Berlin Olympics"] ", the sport was never actually contested at the Games."] "\n\n" [:p {} "However, on 30 November 1939, the Soviet Union attacked Finland, starting the Winter War, formally known as the Russo-Finnish War. The 1940 Olympic Games were canceled late in 1939, with the Finns announcing this in their journal, " [:em {} "Olympic-News Service"] ", in January 1940. The Finns only formally declared their inability to host on 23 April 1940, after the start of Weserübung, the German invasion of Denmark and Norway. " [:a {:href "/athletes/899082"} "De Baillet-Latour"] " officially cancelled the 1940 Olympic Games on 2 May 1940."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Bid process"] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Various cities were interested in hosting the Games: Al-Iskanderiya (Alexandria) (Egypt); Athina (Greece); Barcelona (Spain); Budapest (Hungary); Buenos Aires (Argentina); Dublin (Ireland); Helsinki (Finland); Lausanne (Switzerland); London (England); Montréal (Canada); Rio de Janeiro (Brazil); Roma (Italy); Tokyo (Japan); and Toronto (Canada), but only two bids remained at the bid voting at the 35th " [:a {:href "/meetings"} "IOC Session"] " in Berlin, on 31 July 1936."] "\n\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n  \t" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:th {}] "\n  \t\t" [:th {}] "\n  \t\t" [:th {} "Round 1"] "\n  \t"] [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:td {:class "city"} "Tokyo"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "Japan"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "36"] "\n  \t"] [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:td {:class "city"} "Helsinki"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "Finland"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "27"] "\n  "]]] "\n\n" [:p {} "Tokyo withdrew as hosts of the Games of the XIIth Olympiad on 16 July 1938. The 1940 Olympic Games were awarded to Helsinki on 3 September 1938, at a meeting of the " [:a {:href "/definitions/83"} "IOC Executive Board"] " in Bruxelles, Belgium. After the outbreak of World War II and the Soviet invasion of Finland, Helsinki eventually also withdrew, on 23 April 1940."] "\n\n"] "\n\n\n"] "\n" [:footer {:class "footer"} "\n" [:br {}] "\n" [:div {:class "panel panel-info"} "\n" [:div {:class "panel-heading"} "\n" [:h3 {:class "panel-title"} "\n" [:span {:class "glyphicon glyphicon-info-sign"}] "\nDid you know?\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "panel-body"} "\n" [:p {} "The Tikal brothers " [:a {:href "/athletes/118268"} "Steve Tikal"] " (for Australia) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/98274"} "František Tikal"] " (for Czechoslovakia) faced each other in an ice hockey match at the 1960 Winter Olympics to become the first brothers competing head-to-head for different nations."] "\n\n\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "container"} "\n" [:p {} "\n" [:a {:href "/users/sign_in"} "Login"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/statistics/site"} "Statistics"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/static/about"} "About"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/static/faq"} "FAQ"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/feedbacks/new"} "Feedback"] "\n"] "\n" [:p {} "\n© " [:a {:href "/static/about"} "OlyMADMen"] " 2006 — 2026\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n\n" [:script {:src "/assets/lightbox.min-a06f7b5a37bdc88a78a48f95b9149ca917761a07bffb855a6d73c1a435e16552.js"}] #object[org.jsoup.nodes.TextNode 0x240aeb5e ""] [:script {} "\n  $('.footnote').tooltip();\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n")